  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-06-16T19:43:40.853Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently the VRC_Trigger has a AudioTrigger action which is using the { AudioSource.Play } ( https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/AudioSource.Play.html ) method. Which cuts off audio and replays at the start if its triggered while audio is playing. A new VRC_Trigger action can be added which uses the { AudioSource.PlayOneShot } ( https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/AudioSource.PlayOneShot.html ) method. This would allow for music and SFX to overlay each other with each activation instead of restarting the audio. With the recent midi support this would this would allow for realistic piano playing so you can play a key over and over without it getting messed up and cutting off. This would also help with game SFX for worlds like gun fire or other overlaying audio. I can already trigger the playoneshot() method with a button component but direct VRC_Trigger support would be a lot nicer.",
